 ## Architectural content
 
+TopicMask is the immutable neutral selector for a [Topic](9e2ffa9b4a1d4422a33c2a4bbcfc86ef.md).
+Feature owners govern selection use, disclosure, routing, publication,
+execution and persistence. Themis separately evaluates authorisation.
+A TopicMask has no runtime UUID or natural ordering.
+[Accepted design §§4–8](../../../design/offline-design/DRP-Topic-and-TopicMask.Final.003.md#4-topicmask-kinds-and-matching).
+
+### Kinds, structural equality and construction
+
+An ordinary mask contains at least one ordered criterion and an
+`includeContainedElements` flag, false by default. Each criterion holds
+independent qualifier and value patterns and an optional raw version
+constraint. Ordinary equality and hashing use the original texts in order,
+constraint presence and the containment flag.
+
+The explicit universal kind matches every non-null Topic. Universal masks
+compare equal and carry neither criteria, containment nor an ordinary
+canonical expression. An ordinary mask remains ordinary when its patterns
+cover every valid field. Reject empty, invalid and ambiguous ordinary input
+without inferring universality. Ordinary-only accessors reject a universal
+mask.
+
+Validate immutable entries before adding them. Failed additions and builds
+preserve builder state and prior snapshots. Builders are reusable and
+successful builds publish independent immutable snapshots. Qualifier and
+value patterns must be supplied. An empty pattern cannot match a valid
+nonempty field. Literal helpers validate completed field text before
+escaping it. Mask construction generates no qualifier default.
+
+### Positional evaluation and version constraints
+
+Check depth first. Exact depth requires equal entry counts and inclusive
+containment allows additional trailing entries. At each position, check
+qualifier, value and any version constraint in that order. Stop on the first
+mismatch. A null Topic or unexpected evaluation failure returns false.
+
+Qualifier and value evaluation is case-sensitive on the whole decoded field.
+The six forms are exact, prefix, suffix, contains, non-overlapping prefix
+and suffix, and any valid field. Only an unescaped asterisk is a wildcard.
+Two wildcard operators are valid only around a nonempty contains literal.
+A backslash escapes an asterisk or another backslash in a raw pattern and
+is otherwise literal. Preserve original text and code points. Bounded string
+operations supply the matcher. The accepted contract excludes regex engines.
+
+A missing version constraint is unrestricted and a present-empty one never
+matches. Any explicit constraint fails on an absent candidate version.
+Unmarked text compares literally and case-sensitively. A leading numeric
+operator selects numeric matching and a leading exact-text escape can quote
+a reserved operator or backslash. Literal commas remain exact text.
+Numeric comparisons use nonnegative ASCII dot-separated integer components,
+ignore leading zeroes and compare missing trailing components as zero.
+Compare digit spans without numeric conversion. Nonnumeric candidates fail
+numeric constraints. Runtime Topic identity excludes the opaque version.
+
+Single numeric constraints use equality or inclusive or exclusive comparison.
+Ranges have one lower then one upper comparison, separated by a comma. They
+require valid endpoints in increasing order, or equal endpoints with both
+bounds inclusive. Construction checks endpoint syntax, direction and ordering.
+Matching tests the actual version against both bounds. Reject malformed
+operator-led input before mutation and preserve the raw spelling, including
+any escape, for structural identity and reconstruction.
+
+### Canonical expression and logical interchange
+
+Ordinary masks use `qualifierPattern[:versionConstraint]=valuePattern` in
+ordered dot-separated entries, with a separate containment flag. Escape
+literal period, equals, colon and backslash in the outer layer. Decode that
+layer before interpreting either raw matching grammar. Preserve absence by
+omitting the colon segment and present-empty by emitting a colon with an
+empty field. Strict reconstruction preserves original text and rejects
+malformed delimiters, escapes or constraints.
+
+Logical interchange preserves kind, ordered criteria, containment and version
+presence. Universal records omit criteria and containment. The XML codec uses
+strict UTF-8 and Base64 for the original `qualifierPattern`, `valuePattern`
+and optional `versionConstraint` texts. An absent constraint element and an
+empty decoded element remain distinct. XML decodes raw text directly before
+field validation. Reject unknown structure, encoding conflicts, non-XML
+structural whitespace, DTDs and external resolution. Reconstruct validated
+completed records deterministically.
+
+### Interfaces, limits and governed reuse
+
+The supported Naming surface and strict XML operations are specified in
+[Final.003 §8](../../../design/offline-design/DRP-Topic-and-TopicMask.Final.003.md#8-supported-java-api).
+Parsers, evaluators and optional invocation-local diagnostics are internal.
+Use bounded, safe metadata. Disabled evaluation diagnostics construct and
+dispatch no record. Handler failure preserves the established matching result.
+Application logging and mandatory security audit retain their distinct owners.
+
+Apply the depth, decoded field, pattern, numeric operand, canonical and XML
+bounds of [Final.003 §6](../../../design/offline-design/DRP-Topic-and-TopicMask.Final.003.md#6-resource-limits-concurrency-and-diagnostics).
+Preserve strict validation and fail-closed behaviour. Reconcile affected
+consumers and interchange to this contract under Final.003 §7. A legacy
+engine, selector dialect, parser or dual-format codec is outside this design.
+InformationUnitMask, OperationalMetadataMask, PetasosParcelMask, discovery,
+subscription and other consumers retain their feature-owned criteria and
+governed responsibilities.
